  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 138 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge over central and eastern Texas on Friday will \nshift east into the Mississippi Valley during the weekend. An upper \ntrough will be over the western CONUS on Friday. A cutoff low will \ndevelop in the southern portion of this trough, with the low moving \ninto Arizona on Saturday, and into southwestern Colorado on Sunday. \nWith moistening low-level south-southeast flow, expect an increase \nin cloud cover during the weekend. Temperatures will be pleasant \noverall, albeit 4-7 degrees above normal with morning lows in the \nmid 50s to around 60 and afternoon highs in the mid 70s to lower \n80s.  \n\nAn upper trough over Colorado/New Mexico Sunday evening will move \neast into the central/southern Plains on Monday. Far western \nparts of our area will have a low chance for showers and a few \nthunderstorms Sunday afternoon and evening, and low to medium rain\nchances (20-40 percent) will gradually expand across the \nnorthwest half of our area on Monday. A weak cold front \n(associated with the aforementioned trough) is progged to move \nsouth into our area on Tuesday, and bring a possibility of \nisolated to scattered showers and a few thunderstorms. Increased \ncloud cover will help to limit daytime highs to mostly the mid to \nupper 70s. Temperatures look to be a little cooler behind the \nfront in the Big Country on Tuesday.",
